# Push Arrs Hub to GitHub

When finishing a meaningful chunk of work in this repo (new feature, fix, or multi-file change):

1. Commit the changes with a clear message (do not wait to be asked).
2. Push to `origin` on the current branch (`git push -u origin HEAD` if needed).
3. Never commit `data/`, `.env`, tokens, API keys, or Plex credentials.
4. Skip empty commits. If only secrets/local data changed, do not commit.

Do this at natural stopping points (feature done, bug fixed), not after every tiny edit.
